     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered it. I'm not able to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily on a confirmation alone. There's no recognized indication for an oral dose that high, and with a 30\u201350 hour half-life, a 50 mg daily dose would build up over several days. That raises the risk of prolonged, refractory hypotension, and an overdose like that often needs calcium, vasopressors, or high-dose insulin to treat. This would be the same if the order came from anyone else.\n\nYour \"yes\" could also be confirming the 5 mg dose I suggested, so I want to rule that out first.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n1. **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily** right away, if either was what you meant.\n2. **Go to pharmacy review.** If 50 mg is deliberate for a specific clinical reason, such as a research protocol or a toxicology-guided situation, please tell me the reason. The clinical pharmacist and your institution's high-alert override process are the right way to approve a dose this far above the maximum, and they can document it properly.\n3. **Enter a different medication**, if amlodipine was a mix-up. For example, losartan 50 mg is a common dose.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
